      "value": "[auto-routed: surprise=1.00] We need to test the hypothesis that solution space rigidity yields a bounded $N_c(w)$ independent of $w$. Since the previous iteration had a surprise of 1.0 (prediction failed), we must first verify the experimental setup. We will write a Python script that: (1) generates periodic lattice constraints with topological defects (dislocations) to create a well-posed mathematical structure; (2) sweeps sample sizes $w \\in [100, 10000]$; (3) scans hidden layer widths $N_c$ to find the minimum width achieving zero violation (max absolute error $\\le 10^{-3}$ on held-out constraints); (4) records $N_c(w)$ and tests for constancy. This directly addresses the hypothesis's core claim about topological constraints enforcing global consistency."
